export anchor PDALCDStyle:
    number: 161
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: PDA LCD
    idea: A late 90s handheld organiser in a grey plastic case, with silkscreened app buttons beside a greenish monochrome LCD, inverted title bars, small round ended stylus buttons, pixel glyphs and dotted record lists.
    base: light
    palette:
        desk: #e9e8e3, the page
        case: #b4b8b0, the device body, with light #d3d6cf
        caseDark: #6e726b, seams and button edges
        silk: #2e312c, silkscreen labels and icons on the case
        bezel: #4a4f47, the recess around the screen
        lcd: #c4d0a8, the screen and text on inverted bars
        lcdShade: #b3c095, the inner screen shadow and the focused field
        pixel: #1d2616, all LCD text, bars and inverted rows
        pixelSoft: #3a4630, times and secondary LCD text
    type:
        The LCD uses Lucida Console, Monaco, DejaVu Sans Mono, Courier New,
        monospace with font smoothing off, bold 20px greeting, bold 14px
        pane titles, bold 28px numbers at minus 0.04em, 14px body and 12
        to 13px records and memo. The case uses Helvetica Neue, Arial,
        sans-serif in bold 10 to 12px caps tracked 0.06 to 0.24em.
    layout:
        The whole dashboard lives inside one landscape organiser. The case
        has a printed model name and a power LED on top, a column of six
        lozenge silkscreen buttons with line icons down the left for the
        nav, Home filled dark, and a dark bezel framing the LCD. A stylus
        rests against the right edge. On the screen a black title bar
        carries a Home tab, the name and the date, then a command row with
        Find and an underline field, an inverted New project stylus button,
        a bell count button and User Mara Okafor. The greeting reads Hello,
        Mara. with the date and an inverted Alarm line for the overdue
        tasks. A ruled split makes two panes. The left pane has a four cell
        boxed summary, the overdue cell inverted, then six project records
        with a checkbox, bold name, a code like OK on track, and a line
        with the team, a ten cell segment meter and the facts, the second
        record shown selected in inverse. The right pane has the activity
        memo with short times on the right and a pixel bar graph, dithered
        for last week and solid for this week. Five round hardware buttons
        and an up and down rocker sit under the screen with printed
        labels. Below 980px the panes stack. Below 680px the silkscreen
        buttons move under the screen in a three column grid.
    spacing: A tight 2px grid on the LCD with 5px record padding. The case uses 12 to 22px margins.
    density: Dense like a small pixel screen scaled up. Two panes split by a 1px line.
    corners: The case is 28px on top and 44px at the bottom. Screen 3px. Stylus buttons 8px. Silkscreen buttons are lozenges.
    borders: 1px pixel lines and dotted 1px record separators, 2px under pane titles.
    shadows: Moulded plastic only, a soft case drop, an inset bezel and raised round buttons. None on the LCD.
    icons:
        Hard edged pixel glyphs drawn with crisp edges. A round dot with
        OK means on track, a notched triangle with RISK means at risk, a
        crossed square with LATE means behind, and a bell marks the
        overdue alarm. Line icons sit on the case.
    focus: A 2px pixel outline offset 2px, then a ring of LCD green and a second 2px pixel ring.
    tone: Terse device labels, such as Find, Alarm, Memo, 6 records and yday.
